# Carom — Single player (Solo)

Solo is one of the two ways to play Carom, reached from `SOLO` on the main menu.
It pits player one, the left paddle controlled by the human, against the AI on the
right. Solo and Versus differ in who controls the right paddle: the AI here, a
second human there.

Every figure below carries the name this specification gives it.

## Controls

Keyboard only. The controls are registered actions on the `LAYOUT`
(`dual-vertical`) touch layout. Register exactly the eight names in `ACTIONS`, in
that order, each bound to the keys `BINDINGS` gives it:

| Action | Keys | Does |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `p1-up` | `KeyW` | Moves the human's (left) paddle up. |
| `p1-down` | `KeyS` | Moves the human's (left) paddle down. |
| `p2-up` | `ArrowUp` | Also moves it up: Solo has one human player. |
| `p2-down` | `ArrowDown` | Also moves it down: Solo has one human player. |
| `confirm` | `Enter`, `Space` | Accepts the selected menu item. |
| `back` | `Escape` | Goes back a screen. |
| `pause` | `KeyP`, `Escape` | Pauses at any time. |
| `mute` | `KeyM` | Toggles mute. |

- `W`/`S` and `Up`/`Down` therefore both move the human's paddle, which moves at
  `PADDLE_SPEED` while a movement action is held and is otherwise stationary.
- `back` and `pause` share the `Escape` key. Read `pause` while a match is live
  and `back` on the menus, so `Escape` pauses in a match and goes back on a menu.

The AI drives the right paddle in Solo.

## HUD

- The two scores sit near the top of the field in monospace digits `SCORE_FONT_PX`
  (`76`) tall, drawn in `COLOR.text`: player one's score centered on
  `x = SCORE_P1_X` (`520`) and player two's on `x = SCORE_P2_X` (`760`), with
  their tops at `y = SCORE_TOP_Y` (`40`).
- The mode label `MODE_LABEL.solo` (`SOLO`) sits small and dim, in
  `COLOR.textDim`, in the top-left of the field during a match.

## AI opponent

The AI controls the right paddle in Solo. It is a competent but beatable opponent.

- The AI moves its paddle vertically at a maximum of `AI_SPEED` (`560`) units per
  second, below the human's `PADDLE_SPEED` (`720`), so a well-placed or
  well-curved shot can beat it.
{{#if (eq variant.slug "multi")}}
- The AI defends one ball at a time: of the balls in flight moving toward its
  goal, the one that reaches its paddle soonest. It leaves the other two alone.
- While it has a ball to defend, it tracks that ball's current `y`, reacting with
  the lag time constant `AI_REACT` (`0.12` seconds) and stopping when the paddle
  center is within `AI_DEADZONE` (`10`) units of the target. It tracks the ball's
  present position rather than a predicted one, so a curving shot can get past
  it.
- With no ball flying toward its goal, the AI eases back toward `AI_HOME_Y`
  (`360`, the vertical center).
{{else}}
- When the ball is moving toward the AI, it tracks the ball's current `y`,
  reacting with the lag time constant `AI_REACT` (`0.12` seconds) and stopping
  when the paddle center is within `AI_DEADZONE` (`10`) units of the target. It
  tracks the ball's present position rather than a predicted one, so a curving
  shot can get past it.
- When the ball is moving away, the AI eases back toward `AI_HOME_Y` (`360`, the
  vertical center).
{{/if}}
